From 136bea89db937977810961f380f723a107ffec4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Fischer <info@tobiasfischer.info>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:39:40 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] RITM, DEXTR, the pretrained classifiers and training use the
 Apple GPU: device is CUDA, else MPS, else CPU via genutils.torchDevice
 (TAGLAB_DEVICE overrides); weights load on the CPU; pyramid pooling falls
 back to the CPU where MPS cannot pool; float32 GDL weights; losses follow the
 tensor device. Same masks as the CPU on Goat M1 (IoU 1.0), 3 to 20 times
 faster

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
